WEBVTT

1
00:00:33.708 --> 00:00:36.458
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:45.625
<b>that those who desire worldly success</b>
<b>in return for their actions worship various deities.</b>

3
00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:46.666
<b>Now here,</b>

4
00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:50.000
<b>Lord Krishna takes this subject further.</b>

5
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.250
<b>He explains that even for those who </b>
<b>have material and worldly desires,</b>

6
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:58.166
<b>Lord Krishna has created a system</b>

7
00:00:58.166 --> 00:01:02.291
<b>that not only assists people </b>
<b>in fulfilling their desires</b>

8
00:01:02.291 --> 00:01:09.041
<b>but also presents a direction for </b>
<b>their spiritual development.</b>

9
00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:16.291
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna says,</b>

10
00:01:16.291 --> 00:01:22.958
<b>"According to their qualities and actions, I have </b>
<b>divided human society into four varnas (classes).</b>

11
00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:25.750
<b>I have certainly created this system,</b>

12
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:29.541
<b>but I am not a doer within this system,</b>

13
00:01:29.541 --> 00:01:34.125
<b>nor do I undergo any change </b>
<b>according to this system.</b>

14
00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:39.208
<b>" Lord Krishna wants to say that even </b>
<b>though He is not a part of this system,</b>

15
00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:44.541
<b>He has created it only for </b>
<b>the ease of human society.</b>

16
00:01:44.541 --> 00:01:47.833
<b>We will have to understand this well.</b>

17
00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:51.708
<b>Here Lord Krishna is talking </b>
<b>about the varna system.</b>

18
00:01:51.708 --> 00:01:53.750
<b>As we have understood earlier,</b>

19
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:59.833
<b>human nature is influenced by the three</b>
<b>qualities of sattva, rajas, and tamas,</b>

20
00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:04.625
<b>where sattva symbolizes peace and harmony,</b>

21
00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:05.500
<b>rajas</b>

22
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.291
<b>symbolizes desires and conflict,</b>

23
00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:11.958
<b>and tamas symbolizes laziness and ignorance.</b>

24
00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:13.208
<b>Accordingly,</b>

25
00:02:13.208 --> 00:02:16.791
<b>the human race has been divided into four varnas.</b>

26
00:02:16.791 --> 00:02:17.833
<b>First varna:</b>

27
00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:19.000
<b>Brahmins –</b>

28
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.000
<b>Brahmins are those who are engaged in </b>
<b>the control of the senses and mind,</b>

29
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:29.750
<b>study of scriptures, and providing </b>
<b>spiritual guidance to society.</b>

30
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.041
<b>Second varna:</b>

31
00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:32.333
<b>Kshatriyas –</b>

32
00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:37.000
<b>They handle the responsibilities </b>
<b>of governance, security, and war.</b>

33
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.125
<b>Third varna:</b>

34
00:02:38.125 --> 00:02:39.333
<b>Vaishyas –</b>

35
00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:45.000
<b>They handle agriculture, trade, </b>
<b>animal husbandry, etc.</b>

36
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.125
<b>Fourth varna:</b>

37
00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:47.125
<b>Shudras –</b>

38
00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:55.125
<b>They support the above three varnas and </b>
<b>earn their livelihood through their work skills.</b>

39
00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:58.208
<b>Each varna has its own role and duty,</b>

40
00:02:58.208 --> 00:03:03.708
<b>and it is within these varnas that a human</b>
<b>can also make spiritual progress.</b>

41
00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:09.458
<b>The main point here is that although </b>
<b>Lord Krishna has created this system,</b>

42
00:03:09.458 --> 00:03:10.375
<b>but,</b>

43
00:03:10.375 --> 00:03:14.500
<b>He Himself does not determine </b>
<b>any person's varna.</b>

44
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.583
<b>He is completely impartial.</b>

45
00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:20.000
<b>These varnas are determined according </b>
<b>to people's qualities</b>

46
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:27.875
<b>and according to their aspirations </b>
<b>and consequently, the actions chosen by them.</b>

47
00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:31.291
<b>It is also important to know</b>

48
00:03:31.291 --> 00:03:36.250
<b>that Lord Krishna Himself is far beyond </b>
<b>material qualities and this varna system.</b>

49
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:42.583
<b>In any of His avatars, He may be seen </b>
<b>following the duties of a particular varna,</b>

50
00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:43.416
<b>but</b>

51
00:03:43.416 --> 00:03:45.875
<b>He is neither bound by this,</b>

52
00:03:45.875 --> 00:03:48.500
<b>nor is it any compulsion for Him.</b>

53
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:54.500
<b>He does all this only to set an example for others.</b>

54
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.750
<b>Another extremely important point is that</b>

55
00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:03.583
<b>the varna system being talked </b>
<b>about here is not a caste division.</b>

56
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:09.125
<b>People often misunderstand it as </b>
<b>a caste division and view it negatively.</b>

57
00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:13.333
<b>In modern times, such division </b>
<b>can be seen in every field.</b>

58
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:14.791
<b>In schools,</b>

59
00:04:14.791 --> 00:04:19.416
<b>students are classified according to </b>
<b>their academic performance;</b>

60
00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:22.583
<b>in a professional organization, employees </b>
<b>are divided into classes according to their skills</b>

61
00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:28.666
<b>and work performance and </b>
<b>are given different roles.</b>

62
00:04:28.666 --> 00:04:33.500
<b>All this is also similar to classification </b>
<b>according to qualities and actions.</b>

63
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.750
<b>One purpose of the varna system is </b>
<b>classification according to actions,</b>

64
00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:44.000
<b>and the other purpose is to provide society </b>
<b>with a framework for spiritual progress.</b>

65
00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.791
<b>So that people can improve their qualities </b>
<b>and actions and determine their varna.</b>

66
00:04:49.791 --> 00:04:54.500
<b>And as a person moves from tamas </b>
<b>to rajas, and from rajas to sattva,</b>

67
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.291
<b>he will make spiritual progress.</b>

68
00:04:57.291 --> 00:04:58.458
<b>Lord Krishna</b>

69
00:04:58.458 --> 00:05:03.666
<b>neither interferes in this varna </b>
<b>system nor takes any side.</b>

70
00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:04.583
<b>But</b>

71
00:05:04.583 --> 00:05:11.083
<b>out of His love for mankind, </b>
<b>He has provided such a facility</b>

72
00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:15.125
<b>with the help of which not only </b>
<b>can human life become simple,</b>

73
00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:16.041
<b>but</b>

74
00:05:16.041 --> 00:05:20.833
<b>one also gets the inspiration to </b>
<b>keep making this life excellent.</b>

75
00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:29.416
<b>The varna system mentioned in this verse,</b>

76
00:05:29.416 --> 00:05:34.083
<b>and if this sysytem is understood from the </b>
<b>right perspective,</b>

77
00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:41.208
<b>then it can provide an extremely important </b>
<b>framework for living life.</b>

78
00:05:41.208 --> 00:05:42.708
<b>Fish</b>

79
00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:44.083
<b>cannot walk,</b>

80
00:05:44.083 --> 00:05:45.000
<b>but</b>

81
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.666
<b>no other animal/bird can swim like them;</b>

82
00:05:49.666 --> 00:05:55.958
<b>birds cannot swim, but no one can fly like them.</b>

83
00:05:55.958 --> 00:05:58.958
<b>Every creature, even every tree/plant,</b>

84
00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:05.083
<b>has its own characteristics that </b>
<b>contribute to the environment.</b>

85
00:06:05.083 --> 00:06:09.833
<b>Every human being also has different </b>
<b>abilities, different tendencies,</b>

86
00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:16.500
<b>which determine how they can make </b>
<b>an excellent contribution to society.</b>

87
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.833
<b>For example,</b>

88
00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:22.708
<b>someone has a natural inclination </b>
<b>towards teaching like the Brahmin varna,</b>

89
00:06:22.708 --> 00:06:27.250
<b>while someone else has </b>
<b>leadership skills like a Kshatriya.</b>

90
00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:31.250
<b>Someone is skilled in business </b>
<b>like the Vaishya varna,</b>

91
00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:37.083
<b>while someone else excels in service </b>
<b>and support like the Shudra varna.</b>

92
00:06:37.083 --> 00:06:40.833
<b>This is according to their specific abilities.</b>

93
00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:46.958
<b>When you understand your natural</b>
<b>disposition and especially accept it,</b>

94
00:06:46.958 --> 00:06:50.958
<b>it brings stability and satisfaction in life.</b>

95
00:06:50.958 --> 00:06:53.833
<b>Because in such a case, </b>
<b>whatever work you choose</b>

96
00:06:53.833 --> 00:06:58.250
<b>will match your qualities and your inclination.</b>

97
00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:04.333
<b>This will not only make your work ability </b>
<b>excellent and give you satisfaction,</b>

98
00:07:04.333 --> 00:07:05.041
<b>but</b>

99
00:07:05.041 --> 00:07:09.791
<b>you will also be able to make an</b>
<b>impressive contribution to society.</b>

100
00:07:09.791 --> 00:07:11.291
<b>For example,</b>

101
00:07:11.291 --> 00:07:14.541
<b>if your interest is in analyzing numbers</b>

102
00:07:14.541 --> 00:07:18.666
<b>or deeply understanding a subject,</b>

103
00:07:18.666 --> 00:07:23.541
<b>you can be successful in the </b>
<b>path of education or research.</b>

104
00:07:23.541 --> 00:07:24.333
<b>On the other hand,</b>

105
00:07:24.333 --> 00:07:28.833
<b>if your decision-making power is</b>
<b>strong and you are self-confident,</b>

106
00:07:28.833 --> 00:07:34.666
<b>then leading others will also be natural </b>
<b>and appropriate for you.</b>

107
00:07:34.666 --> 00:07:42.208
<b>You also know that when a </b>
<b>task is against your nature,</b>

108
00:07:42.208 --> 00:07:46.666
<b>it only gives birth to stress and dissatisfaction.</b>

109
00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:47.875
<b>For example,</b>

110
00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:51.541
<b>if your interest and inclination is in sports,</b>

111
00:07:51.541 --> 00:07:52.625
<b>but</b>

112
00:07:52.625 --> 00:07:59.625
<b>you are forced to become a doctor, </b>
<b>then you will always live in dissatisfaction.</b>

113
00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:02.291
<b>Both are important for society –</b>

114
00:08:02.291 --> 00:08:03.416
<b>a sportsperson,</b>

115
00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:05.708
<b>who brings honor to the country,</b>

116
00:08:05.708 --> 00:08:09.333
<b>gives encouragement and </b>
<b>entertainment to others,</b>

117
00:08:09.333 --> 00:08:14.458
<b>and also a doctor who improves others' health.</b>

118
00:08:14.458 --> 00:08:19.333
<b>All varnas have their own importance, </b>
<b>all varnas have satisfaction; </b>

119
00:08:19.333 --> 00:08:25.791
<b>the only requirement is that you </b>
<b>need to identify your varna.</b>

120
00:08:25.791 --> 00:08:27.791
<b>Recognize your nature,</b>

121
00:08:27.791 --> 00:08:31.750
<b>know your abilities, and accepting them,</b>

122
00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:35.333
<b>move forward in life accordingly.</b>

123
00:08:39.916 --> 00:08:44.208
<b>Understanding this varna system </b>
<b>from the right perspective</b>

124
00:08:44.208 --> 00:08:48.291
<b>is also extremely useful for a family.</b>

125
00:08:48.291 --> 00:08:53.041
<b>Each member of the family has </b>
<b>unique qualities and characteristics.</b>

126
00:08:53.041 --> 00:08:57.083
<b>And it is important for the elders </b>
<b>of the family to recognize and</b>

127
00:08:57.083 --> 00:09:04.208
<b>encourage these characteristics </b>
<b>in family members.</b>

128
00:09:04.208 --> 00:09:06.458
<b>For example,</b>

129
00:09:06.458 --> 00:09:11.666
<b>if someone is eager to gain knowledge </b>
<b>like the Brahmin varna,</b>

130
00:09:11.666 --> 00:09:16.416
<b>then he can be successful in </b>
<b>educational roles in the future.</b>

131
00:09:16.416 --> 00:09:17.625
<b>Similarly,</b>

132
00:09:17.625 --> 00:09:22.375
<b>someone else who is firm and </b>
<b>courageous in making decisions</b>

133
00:09:22.375 --> 00:09:28.291
<b>would be suitable in a leadership </b>
<b>role like the Kshatriya varna.</b>

134
00:09:28.291 --> 00:09:34.500
<b>If you force someone to do a job </b>
<b>contrary to their inclination,</b>

135
00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:39.166
<b>it will only create stress and dissatisfaction.</b>

136
00:09:39.166 --> 00:09:40.375
<b>For example,</b>

137
00:09:40.375 --> 00:09:47.333
<b>if a person with a calm nature is pushed</b>
<b>into a highly competitive business,</b>

138
00:09:47.333 --> 00:09:53.416
<b>it will not only adversely affect their </b>
<b>work efficiency and mental state</b>

139
00:09:53.416 --> 00:09:54.333
<b>but</b>

140
00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:59.000
<b>will also have the opposite effect on the family.</b>

141
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.333
<b>It is natural</b>

142
00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:07.416
<b>that a person who is facing extreme stress</b>
<b>in their work or business day after day</b>

143
00:10:07.416 --> 00:10:13.625
<b>will definitely have a negative impact of </b>
<b>this stress on their family relationships as well.</b>

144
00:10:13.625 --> 00:10:20.916
<b>In such a situation, will that person be able </b>
<b>to take out time for meditation and spirituality?</b>

145
00:10:20.916 --> 00:10:22.750
<b>No, right?</b>

146
00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:28.791
<b>Help family members recognize </b>
<b>their natural qualities,</b>

147
00:10:28.791 --> 00:10:31.875
<b>encourage them in this direction.</b>

148
00:10:31.875 --> 00:10:37.958
<b>By doing so, you are not only contributing </b>
<b>to their personal well-being</b>

149
00:10:37.958 --> 00:10:38.916
<b>but</b>

150
00:10:38.916 --> 00:10:42.458
<b>family relationships will also become sweet.</b>

151
00:10:42.458 --> 00:10:45.208
<b>And by creating such a happy family,</b>

152
00:10:45.208 --> 00:10:50.791
<b>you are also laying the foundation </b>
<b>for the spiritual progress of all.</b>

153
00:10:56.791 --> 00:11:04.000
<b>There is a lot to learn from this varna system</b>
<b>in the professional environment.</b>

154
00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:08.458
<b>In any organization, it is extremely important</b>

155
00:11:08.458 --> 00:11:13.375
<b>that a suitable employee is selected for each job.</b>

156
00:11:13.375 --> 00:11:21.166
<b>And this depends on the employee's abilities, </b>
<b>their interests, and their nature.</b>

157
00:11:21.166 --> 00:11:28.458
<b>This is similar to how one's varna</b>
<b>is determined according to one's inclination.</b>

158
00:11:28.458 --> 00:11:30.083
<b>For example,</b>

159
00:11:30.083 --> 00:11:32.875
<b>like the Brahmin varna, if a person</b>

160
00:11:32.875 --> 00:11:38.416
<b>is interested in knowledge </b>
<b>and understanding every subject in detail,</b>

161
00:11:38.416 --> 00:11:40.000
<b>then such an employee</b>

162
00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:45.875
<b>would be suitable for research or </b>
<b>the planning department of the organization.</b>

163
00:11:45.875 --> 00:11:46.750
<b>On the other hand,</b>

164
00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:48.541
<b>like the Kshatriya varna,</b>

165
00:11:48.541 --> 00:11:52.041
<b>a person with leadership and </b>
<b>decision-making abilities</b>

166
00:11:52.041 --> 00:11:57.125
<b>will be able to smoothly direct</b>
<b>a group of employees.</b>

167
00:11:57.125 --> 00:12:00.583
<b>Whether it is conducting research individually,</b>

168
00:12:00.583 --> 00:12:03.708
<b>having the responsibility of </b>
<b>leading other employees,</b>

169
00:12:03.708 --> 00:12:07.583
<b>taking care of the financial profit </b>
<b>of the organization, or</b>

170
00:12:07.583 --> 00:12:15.375
<b>managing the human resources department </b>
<b>in the form of assistance to people</b>

171
00:12:15.375 --> 00:12:19.791
<b>working in all these positions, all these are</b>
<b>important for an organization.</b>

172
00:12:19.791 --> 00:12:22.208
<b>And if you look at it,</b>

173
00:12:22.208 --> 00:12:30.166
<b>this division is also similar to the </b>
<b>Brahmin, Kshatriya, Vaishya, and Shudra varnas.</b>

174
00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:36.541
<b>To implement this appropriately, </b>
<b>these four things are necessary:</b>

175
00:12:36.541 --> 00:12:37.625
<b>First -</b>

176
00:12:37.625 --> 00:12:40.291
<b>Recognize people's inclinations</b>

177
00:12:40.291 --> 00:12:41.250
<b>Second -</b>

178
00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.958
<b>Assign them work according to that inclination</b>

179
00:12:44.958 --> 00:12:45.708
<b>Third -</b>

180
00:12:45.708 --> 00:12:49.000
<b>Provide them training regularly</b>

181
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.166
<b>Fourth -</b>

182
00:12:50.166 --> 00:12:53.416
<b>Show interest in their progress</b>

183
00:12:53.416 --> 00:12:57.125
<b>When you assign appropriate work to people,</b>

184
00:12:57.125 --> 00:13:01.583
<b>show interest in their training and progress,</b>

185
00:13:01.583 --> 00:13:08.166
<b>then ultimately the organization</b>
<b>will benefit from it.</b>

186
00:13:08.166 --> 00:13:09.833
<b>Think about it.</b>

